0.5.1f:
- [x] Fix: the `/login` magic-link handler now forwards `?llm_model=` through its post-auth redirect. The 0.5.1b client honors `?llm_model=` on the chat page, but the server-side magic-link redirect only forwarded an allowlist (`prompt`, `conversation`, `welcome_prompt`) and silently dropped `llm_model` — so every funnel hand-off that goes through `/login?token=…&llm_model=…` (e.g. the mothership picture-to-html flow) lost the model pin and ran the auto-build on the image-blind default DeepSeek. One-line fix: add `llm_model` to the allowlist in `app/routers/ui.py`. Regression test in `app/tests/test_auth_session.py` asserts all hand-off params (incl. `llm_model`) survive the redirect and `token` does not leak.

0.5.1e:
- [x] Bump LangChain version that supports way more efficient checkpoints that don't take up so much disk space. Adopted LangGraph **DeltaChannel** (beta, langgraph 1.2): the `messages` channel now stores an incremental delta per checkpoint + a periodic snapshot instead of re-serializing the whole message list every checkpoint (~O(N) storage instead of O(N^2) — LangChain benchmarks ~41x less). Stack bump (deliberate, together): langgraph 1.2.2→1.2.5 (DeltaChannel correctness fixes), langgraph-checkpoint-postgres 3.0.4→3.1.0 (delta-aware saver), langgraph-sdk 0.3.6→0.4.2, langchain-core 1.4.6→1.4.7, orjson 3.10.18→3.11.9 (resolution verified clean). Opted the whole RailsAgentState fleet + the llamabot agent into DeltaChannel via a shared `messages` annotation (`app/agents/utils/delta_state.py`). Reworked `checkpoint_cleanup.py`: the old aggressive "keep only the latest checkpoint" trim would destroy a delta chain (reconstruction replays ancestor writes back to the nearest snapshot), so post-run cleanup is now gated on `graph_uses_delta_channel(app)` — skipped for delta agents (history retained cheaply, which also restores continue/time-travel), kept for legacy non-delta agents; the periodic sweep is now orphan-only (deletes only writes/blobs with no surviving parent checkpoint). Coverage in `app/tests/test_checkpoint_cleanup_delta.py`.

0.5.1g:
- [x] Enable the ability to register an agent mode with custom tool calls via langgraph.json in a Leonardo project, and select that agent mode through the chat interface. The chat mode dropdown was hardcoded in two image-baked places (`chat.html` `<option>`s + `config.js` `agentModes`), so a per-instance custom agent could never appear without rebuilding the image. Now: an optional per-instance overlay `agent_modes.json` (mounted next to the editable `langgraph.json`) declares custom modes `[{key,label,agent_name,description?,shortLabel?,icon?}]`; `app/routers/ui.py` `load_custom_agent_modes()` validates each entry against the registered `langgraph.json` graphs (drops unregistered `agent_name`s and built-in-key shadows) and injects `window.LLAMABOT_CUSTOM_AGENT_MODES`, also extending the engineer-role default `visible_agents` with the new keys. Frontend: `chat.html` appends the custom `<option>`s before the visibility filter; `config.js` `getAgentModeMap()` merges custom `key→agent_name` under the built-ins (built-ins win); `AppState.setAgentMode` resolves through it. Fully back-compat (no overlay → identical behavior; unknown `agent_name` still collapses to `DEFAULT_AGENT` via the Rails `ROUTABLE_AGENTS` guard). Recipe: `docs/custom-agent-modes.md`. Tests: `app/tests/test_custom_agent_modes.py` (validation core + chat-route injection/visibility integration).

0.5.1h:
- [x] Fix: ticket mode's "implement this ticket?" Yes/No offer didn't consistently appear (reported on Lohman, 0.5.1c). The offer is driven by the `offer_implementation` tool, which calls `interrupt()` to surface the buttons — but it only fires if the LLM actually emits that structured tool call after `write_final_ticket` succeeds. The default ticket-mode model (`deepseek-v4-flash`) only does so ~2/3 of the time; the rest of the time it ends the turn in prose ("Would you like me to switch to engineer mode?") with no tool call, so no interrupt fires and the user never sees the buttons (sometimes the call leaks as raw JSON text). Reproduced against the live DeepSeek model: ~1/3 silent-failure rate, worse on long/post-summarization threads. Fix removes the dependency on that second LLM decision: new `EnsureImplementationOfferMiddleware` (`after_model`/`aafter_model`) detects "a `write_final_ticket` succeeded but the turn ended without an `offer_implementation` call" and deterministically injects the `offer_implementation` tool call — reconstructing `ticket_id`/`title`/`content` from the write call + success ToolMessage. `offer_implementation` is replay-safe (interrupts before any side effect), so forcing it reproduces the happy path exactly (interrupt → buttons → on resume the model sees the decision). Idempotent (won't double-offer if the model already offered or an offer already resolved) and inert when the write failed (markdown-fallback path) or no ticket exists. Tests: `app/tests/test_ensure_implementation_offer.py`.

