0.5.1j:
- [x] Add Alibaba **Qwen3-VL Plus** (the full vision model) as a selectable model, via the official Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope) API. Wired through the existing model machinery: `get_llm("qwen3-vl-plus")` in `llm_factory.py` returns a `ChatQwen` (from the dedicated `langchain-qwq` client) with `enable_thinking=True` + `thinking_budget=8192` and tool calling on by default; `api_base` defaults to the **US (Virginia)** endpoint `https://dashscope-us.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1` (overridable via `ALIBABA_BASE_URL`) and reads `ALIBABA_API_KEY`. Region keys are NOT interchangeable — the base_url must match the key's region. Registered in `model_capabilities.py` (`{images, video}` true, `pdf` false), gated in `/api/available-models` on `ALIBABA_API_KEY`, and added to the chat dropdown (`chat.html`). Chose `ChatQwen` over a bare `ChatOpenAI`-with-base_url because the generic OpenAI client silently drops Qwen's non-standard `reasoning_content`, so thinking would never surface in the UI. That choice forced a deliberate, CI-gated LangChain stack bump (langchain-qwq needs langchain-openai>=1.1.14): langchain-openai 1.0.0→1.3.2, openai 2.2.0→2.43.0, langsmith 0.4.8→0.8.17, langchain-core 1.4.7→1.4.8, Pygments 2.19.1→2.20.0, requests 2.32.5→2.34.2, urllib3 2.4.0→2.7.0, jiter 0.9.0→0.15.0, typing_extensions 4.13.2→4.15.0, + new json-repair 0.53.1 (clean `docker compose build` verified). Live-verified against us-east-1: thinking (reasoning_content populated), tool calling, and vision (image_url) all working. Tests: `app/tests/test_model_capabilities_api.py` locks the Qwen capability row; full `tests/` suite green (201 passed). Also verified the real app transport path (base64 data-URI, both PNG and JPEG, as built by `_build_message_content`) against qwen3-vl-plus — not just remote image URLs.
- [x] Fix: uploading an image while **Qwen3-VL Plus** was selected spuriously auto-switched the user to Gemini ("image → HTML" flow). The frontend image auto-switch keys off a seeded `modelCapabilities` map (so it's correct on the first send, before the async `/api/available-models` fetch resolves), but that seed only listed the text-only DeepSeek models — so Qwen's image-capability was known only after the fetch, and a stale/missing fetch (incl. the no-Python-hot-reload window after the flash→plus swap) left it bounced to the `IMAGE_MODEL`. Seeded `qwen3-vl-plus: { images: true }` in `app/frontend/chat/index.js` so it's image-verified at page load, independent of fetch timing.
- [x] Add the ability to view a modal that shows all imported attachments, and preview the excel sheets.

0.5.1k:
- [x] Add a way to disable/enable models centrally, beyond just whether an API key is present — controllable by mothership and `.env`, not by the instance user. New `app/agents/leonardo/model_policy.py` resolves the permitted-model set from operator-controlled sources only — the mothership-provisioned `.leonardo/instance.json` (`enabled_models` / `disabled_models` arrays, authoritative) and the `ENABLED_MODELS` / `DISABLED_MODELS` env vars (comma-separated, baked into the container) — never from a DB/user-writable setting. Layered resolution, most-specific wins: (1) **explicit disable** (`disabled_models` / `DISABLED_MODELS`, unioned across sources) turns a model OFF and beats everything below; (2) two **fail-open defaults**, `deepseek-v4-flash` (project default text model) and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` (the image auto-switch target), stay globally enabled so every instance always keeps a working text *and* vision model, surviving any allow-list — turned off only by an explicit disable; (3) an **allow-list** (`enabled_models` / `ENABLED_MODELS`, intersected across sources so neither can broaden the other) restricts everything else when configured; (4) with nothing configured the policy is inert and every model stays enabled (key-gated as before). The real enforcement is in `get_llm()` — a model disabled by policy is swapped for an enabled one *before any client is built* — because the websocket `llm_model` field is unvalidated user input, so the dropdown alone would be bypassable. `/api/available-models` reflects the same rule (`available: false`, `reason: "Disabled by administrator"`) so disabled models grey out in the chat picker. Lockout-proof: `enabled_default_model()` always returns a usable model (the fail-open defaults, else the first enabled known model, else the project default) even if the policy is misconfigured to disable everything, so the instance can never be locked out of chat. `.env`/`instance.json` are read at startup, so changes apply on next container recreate (a live mothership push without restart is a possible follow-up). Tests: `app/tests/test_model_policy.py` (fail-open defaults, allow-list intersection, disable-override precedence + union, lockout guard, get_llm enforcement, and the available-models reflection).
- [x] Change Qwen3 default model to 3.7 Plus. Swapped the selectable Qwen model from `qwen3-vl-plus` to Alibaba's `qwen3.7-plus` (the low-cost multimodal agent model: text/image/video, 1M context, GA 2026-06-01) across `llm_factory.py` (ChatQwen, same US-Virginia base + `ALIBABA_API_KEY`, `enable_thinking`/`thinking_budget=8192`), `model_capabilities.py` (`{images,video}` true, `pdf` false — unchanged, still multimodal), `api.py` model→key gating, the chat dropdown (`chat.html`, label "Qwen3.7 Plus"), and the frontend image-capability seed (`index.js`). Also updated the stale `qwen3-vl-plus` entry in `model_policy.py`'s `_KNOWN_MODELS` fallback list. Test renamed to `test_qwen3_7_plus_supports_images_and_video` in `test_model_capabilities_api.py` (5 passed). Live-verified: `get_llm("qwen3.7-plus")` builds and a real base64 data-URI image invoke against the US-Virginia endpoint returns a correct vision answer (region key matches). Gotcha: the dev-box uvicorn runs WITHOUT `--reload`, so Python edits are NOT hot-reloaded — after this swap the still-running server had no `qwen3.7-plus` branch in `get_llm`, fell through to the DeepSeek default, and DeepSeek rejected the image content block (`400 unknown variant image_url`). Fix is to `docker compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml up -d --force-recreate llamabot` after any Python change; the mounted `app/` only hot-reloads Rails, not the FastAPI process.
- [x] Add browser inspect tool into the engineering mode (including adding Playwright/chromium in the docker image). Gives Leo better ability to debug in engineer mode
- [x] Add ability to import .xml files through the browser attach tool, in general, we allow more files to be uploaded through the Leo file import interface

