0.5.1m:
- [x] Fix: assistant messages reported to the mothership were missing `tool_calls` — 0 of 155,343 `InstanceMessage` rows had a non-nil `tool_calls` column, so tool-only turns (empty `content`) rendered as blank rows on the mothership's message-review page. Root cause: `MothershipClient.report_message()` had no `tool_calls` parameter and the call site in `request_handler.py` never passed one. Fix adds the parameter + payload key to `mothership_client.py` and passes `message.tool_calls` (LangChain's already-normalized `{name, args, id}` shape) at the assistant report call site — using `message.tool_calls` instead of `additional_kwargs.tool_calls` (raw OpenAI `{function: {name, arguments}}` shape) so the mothership's `InstanceMessage#tool_call_names` helper can read `tc["name"]` without a Rails-side change. Mothership receiving end was already ready (`tool_calls` jsonb column, `with_tool_calls` scope, `normalized_tool_calls` in the controller). Tests: `app/tests/test_mothership_client.py` (3 unit tests: payload includes key with normalized shape, omitted on None, omitted on empty list).

0.5.1n:
- [x] Report ToolMessage observations to the mothership — sequel to 0.5.1m's `tool_calls` reporting. Adds `tool_call_id: Optional[str]` to `MothershipClient.report_message()` (wire contract: the key is only sent when non-None). Adds module-level `_report_tool_messages()` helper to `request_handler.py` that iterates the node's message list, finds `LCToolMessage` instances, and fires one `report_message(role="tool", content=str(msg.content), tool_call_id=..., tool_calls=[{name, tool_call_id, agent_depth}])` per ToolMessage — verbatim, no truncation. Unlike assistant turns (gated `if not is_subagent`), sub-agent tool outputs are reported too, tagged with `agent_depth` so the mothership can filter. Mothership-side receiver changes (role validation, `tool_call_id` column, views) are Mother Leo's responsibility and must deploy before this image rolls. PR notes the coordination requirement. Tests: `app/tests/test_tool_output_reporting.py` (8 tests: payload contract, no truncation, tool_call_id omitted when None, no double-report, non-ToolMessages ignored, sub-agent tagging).
- [x] Fix: summarization model falls back to DeepSeek when no Gemini key — all four agent nodes (`rails_user_mode_agent`, `rails_ticket_mode_agent`, `rails_plan_mode_agent`, `rails_user_feedback_agent`) instantiated `ChatGoogleGenerativeAI` directly at graph-compile time; a missing `GOOGLE_API_KEY`/`GEMINI_API_KEY` caused every chat request to fail fleet-wide (SupportIncident #93). Fix adds `make_summarization_model()` to `llm_factory.py` as the single source of truth — prefers Gemini 3 Flash when a Google key is present, falls back to DeepSeek v4 Flash + `tiktoken_token_counter` (text-only, no Gemini API calls) + a 60K `trim_tokens_to_summarize` guard otherwise. Also adds `tiktoken_token_counter` to `token_counter.py`. All four agent nodes now call `make_summarization_model()` and unpack `(model, token_counter, trim)`. PR #61.
- [x] Add tool call output into telemetry to track full LLM agent trajectories & traces

