0.5.1p:
- [x] Add the 7th grade vocab into engineer mode, similar to Beginner Mode. Added a user-facing "How You Talk" section to `rails_agent/prompts.py` — a tier softer than Beginner Mode: where Beginner *bans* the basics, Engineer Mode *allows* them sparingly with a plain-English gloss in parentheses on first use (even "database table" / "browser" / "JavaScript" / "back-end"), and *scales up* to match the user's vocabulary if they show they know more. 7th-grade reading level by default; assumes zero knowledge past a handful of primitives (browser, database table, HTML, JS front-end, Ruby back-end) and nothing about Rails/Hotwire/Turbo. All the deep engineering sections stay verbatim — they're flagged as internal "how to build, not how to talk."
- [x] Add Plan Mode for Engineer Mode in AskUserQuestion. New `rails_engineer_plan_mode_agent` — the engineering counterpart to Beginner Plan Mode. Same plan-first 6-phase workflow (Clarify → Research → Refine → Present Plan → Implement → Verify) driven by `ask_user_question` one-question-at-a-time, but retains full Engineer Mode depth. Prompt is composed DRY: a plan-first preamble + Engineer Mode's whole playbook (`RAILS_AGENT_PROMPT`), so the softened voice flows through automatically and there's one source of truth for the engineering knowledge. Routing: when base mode = Engineer and the Plan execution toggle is on, `index.js` routes to the new agent; Beginner and every other mode keep `rails_plan_mode_agent` unchanged. Registered in `app/langgraph.json`; reuses the plan-mode interaction tools (`ask_user_question`, `ask_user_uiux_question`) and summarization prompt verbatim. Tests: `app/tests/test_engineer_plan_mode.py` (voice section present + depth retained, agent registered + importable, prompt composition, plan-tool wiring).


0.5.1q:
- [x] Chat: honor an `?agent_mode=` URL param on the chat page — pin the agent-mode dropdown to the requested persona (validated against the real dropdown options), push it into the live agent config (`AppState.setAgentMode`), and persist it to the session `agentMode` cookie, so a funnel can hand users off in a specific mode instead of the Beginner-mode default. Built for the excel-to-app funnel, which is being rewritten to instant-claim a Leo and kick off a real build in **Engineer mode** (`rails_agent`) — an eval showed engineer-mode builds a genuinely better app (Projects + Price Book from the user's real costs/quote) than the old `stream_html` one-shot. Mirrors the existing `?llm_model=` handling exactly: new `checkAgentModeParam()` in `app/frontend/chat/index.js`, called right after `checkModelParam()` on init (after cookie-restore so the URL param wins, before the `?prompt=` auto-send so the first message routes to the chosen agent). Unknown keys are ignored (incl. per-instance custom modes absent from this dropdown) and the param is stripped from the URL after load so a refresh can't re-apply it after a manual switch. Browser-smoke coverage added in Leonardo e2e (`smoke.spec.ts`). Pairs with the mothership baking `?agent_mode=engineer` into the magic-link redirect — so this also adds `agent_mode` to the `/login` redirect forward-allowlist in `app/routers/ui.py` (same gap 0.5.1f fixed for `llm_model`: the magic-link hand-off goes through `/login?token=…&agent_mode=…`, and the allowlist would otherwise silently drop it before the chat page ever sees it). Regression coverage in `app/tests/test_auth_session.py`.

- [x] Fix: on the feedback **new/edit form** you could only attach multiple images by shift/ctrl-clicking them all inside one file-picker dialog — picking a second file in a second trip through the picker silently replaced the first. Cause: a bare `<input type="file" multiple>` REPLACES its `files` list every time the picker closes. The comment/reply boxes on the feedback show page already solved this (merge each pick into what's staged, plus thumbnails and a per-file remove button), but that logic lived inline in `show.html.erb` and the form never got it. Extracted it verbatim into a shared partial `app/views/llama_bot_rails/user_feedbacks/_attachment_staging_js.html.erb` (gem), now rendered by both `show.html.erb` and `_form.html.erb`; the form's file field opts in with `data-preview-target` + `onchange="mergePickedAttachments(this)"` and gained a preview strip. The show page's zoom modal is now called through a `typeof openImageModal === 'function'` guard since the form pages don't have one; paste-to-attach (Cmd/Ctrl+V into any text box in the form) comes along with the shared script. Tests: `spec/controllers/llama_bot_rails/user_feedbacks_attachment_staging_spec.rb` (render_views on new/edit/show — 4 of its 5 examples fail without the fix). Browser-verified against the real edit form: two separate picker trips → both files staged, remove button drops only the clicked one, submit persists both alongside the existing attachments.

